   "text": "I read the drawing as a head-to-side-chain cyclic pentapeptide, with the Asn \u03b1-NH acylated by a succinyl group that links to the Lys side-chain amine.\n\n**Sequence and ring closure**\n- The ring runs Asn \u2192 Ile \u2192 Pro \u2192 benzothienylalanine (Bta) \u2192 Lys, with a C-terminal primary amide on Lys.\n- Asn keeps its side-chain primary amide.\n- The Lys \u03b5-NH is acylated by a succinyl linker (C(=O)CH\u2082CH\u2082C(=O)), whose other end acylates the Asn \u03b1-NH.\n\n**Substituents**\n- The Pro ring carries a 1,2,3-triazol-1-yl group at C4. The triazole bears a 4-(thiophen-2-yl)phenyl group at its C4.\n- The Bta side chain is CH\u2082 attached at C3 of a benzothiophene.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\nI assigned each centre from the wedge or hash and the substituent positions in the drawing:\n\n| Centre | Assignment |\n|---|---|\n| Asn \u03b1 | S |\n| Ile \u03b1 | S |\n| Ile \u03b2 | S |\n| Pro \u03b1 | S |\n| Pro C4 (triazole carbon) | S |\n| Bta \u03b1 | S |\n| Lys \u03b1 | S |\n\nI then converted each assignment into @/@@ using the neighbour order in the SMILES. The ring-closure digits were checked and the SMILES accounts for every atom in the drawing.\n\nSMILES: O=C1CCC(=O)NCCCC[C@@H](C(N)=O)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc2csc3ccccc23)NC(=O)[C@@H]2C[C@H](n3cc(-c4ccc(-c5cccs5)cc4)nn3)CN2C(=O)[C@H]([C@@H](C)CC)NC(=O)[C@H](CC(N)=O)N1"
